   "InfoDisplay_102176810_Title": "Invoice",
   "InfoDisplay_102181701_Text": "<b>[VERY URGENT! LOST STUDENT ID!!!]</b>\nI lost my student ID on the train yesterday at around 4:30 PM. It's in a soft blue silicone case, and the top-left corner is chipped. This is the fourth student ID I've lost this year. And just thinking about how my professor screamed, collapsed, and yanked out handfuls of her own hair while helping me replace the last one… I honestly don't have the courage to ask her again. If anyone finds it, please contact me or just drop it off at the station's Lost and Found. THANK YOU SO MUCH!!!\n\n[From \"ChangeTheWorldWithLightEnergySciences\"]\n…So you lost your ID again? Also, what do you mean \"screamed, collapsed, and yanked out handfuls of her hair\"? It paints a vivid image, but since when have I ever done that?\nStop looking. You have a project. I already requisitioned a replacement. <b>This is the last one</b>. Come get it.\n\n[From LostStudentID]\nP-Professor?! Um... maybe I should wait a few more days? Someone might find it… no need to trouble you…\n\n[From \"ChangeTheWorldWithLightEnergySciences\"]\nThink again. My office. Now.",
   "InfoDisplay_102181702_Text": "<b>[WARNING: If You Find It, DO NOT Eat It!]</b>\nYesterday around 6:30 AM on my way to the Institute, I accidentally dropped a sample. It's in a transparent bag and looks kind of like Midnight Wonder Cup Noodles. \nIF YOU FIND IT, CONTACT ME IMMEDIATELY! REPEAT: DO NOT CONSUME!\n\n[From \"FoodAndResearchAreMyLife\"]\nOh no… I already ate it. Thought it was cup noodles my labmate left me. Is it toxic?? Bio, mineral, synthetic neuro-??? Do I call medical or start drafting my will??\n\n[From DoNotEatIt]\n…It's not toxic. I spent over a month making that stuff, added a customized nutrient mix, and in previous animal tests it helped control weight and temporarily boosted physical metrics. But the synthesis yield was abysmal. That was the only cup… and I was planning to test it on myself.\n\n[From \"FoodAndResearchAreMyLife\"]\nAh... I see. Sorry, I was starving after an all-nighter.\n\n\n[From DoNotEatIt]\nThen congratulations, you're now the test subject. Send me your weight and grip strength data every 72 hours.\n\n[From \"FoodAndResearchAreMyLife\"]\nCopy that.",
