   "shengtai_LZZQ_1_1": "Spacetrek Collective Research Institute - Field Report (Archived)\n\nResearch Topic: Dynamic Characteristics of the Tacet Discord \"Inferno Rider\" and its Vehicle \nResearch Location: Huanglong — Port City of Guixu \nRelated Projects: Iterative R&D of the Expedition Motorbike Prototype\n\nI. Background\n\nA powerful Tacet Discord, designated \"Inferno Rider,\" has been observed near the Port City of Guixu in Huanglong. The vehicle it utilizes operates with remarkable stability in post-Lament environments. Its structural design and movement patterns are expected to provide critical reference points for the development of our prototype expedition motorbike.\nII. Field Records\n\nLocation: Port City of Guixu — Overpass Ruins\nBy deploying sensors to capture kinetic data, we have determined that the \"Inferno Rider\" performs well above average in the following areas:\n· Control response logic at high speeds.\n· Maneuverability across uneven terrain.\n\nIII. Technical Applications\n\nBy reverse-engineering its movement patterns and structural features, the engineering team has implemented the following improvements to the expedition motorbike prototype:\n……………………\n\n<b>Researcher‘s Handwritten Note:</b>\n<b>The prototype is finished. I never imagined old tech from my hometown all those years ago would find a new life in an expedition motorbike.</b>\n\n<b>Even now, the mention of the \"Inferno Rider\" still strikes fear into people's hearts. I cannot erase the shadow cast by that Tacet Discord, nor can I truly give rest to the souls who perished long ago. At the very least, this prototype proves that our ancestors left more than just pain and terror behind.</b>\n\n<b>They also had hope for the future.</b>\n\n<b>This bike will carry forth their will, guarding the path for those who dare to explore.</b>",
   "shengtai_LZZQ_2_1": "A holographic projection of the \"Inferno Rider,\" likely used as reference material during the prototyping stages of the expedition motorbike.",
   "shengtai_LZZQ_2_2": "Beside it lies a blueprint of the original design. Although the motorbike has undergone several iterations, its original appearance remains significant to this day.",
